e outcomes are in scope.** \\"Radar's documented config shape is not accepted by this Claude Desktop build\\" and \\"this needs a newer/older app version\\" are legitimate root causes. Do not force the cause into my file if the evidence points upstream.\\n>\\n> **Edit protocol**\\n> - Show me the proposed diff. Do not write to disk until I approve.\\n> - Back up to `claude_desktop_config.json.bak` before any write.\\n> - Do not modify entries other than `radar`.\\n>\\n> **Done means:** Claude Desktop restarts with no \\"skipped\\" warning, `radar` appears in the MCP server list, and one tool call against it succeeds. Give me the verification command and the expected output.\\n>\\n> **If you are missing something you need, stop and ask.** A blocked analysis naming the missing input is a better answer than a complete one built on a guess.\\n\\n**What changed and why**\\n\\n| Change | Removes | Targets |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Config paste mandatory, including working entries | N1, N7 | S1, S3 |\\n| Provenance field | N3 | S1, S6 |\\n| Transport question surfaced explicitly | N4 | S1, S6 |\\n| OS/version/path fields | N2 | S5 |\\n| Protocol spelled out as 5 ordered steps with a stop condition | N5 | S3, S4 |\\n| Source hierarchy split host-side vs. vendor-side | N6 | S6 |\\n| \\"Vendor-side outcomes in scope\\" | N6 | S6 |\\n| `UNVERIFIED` labeling requirement | N1 | S1 |\\n| Diff-then-approve + backup + scope limit | N8 | destructive-write path |\\n| Explicit done criteria + verification command | N9 | S2 |\\n| Marketing blurb cut to one line | N4 | token efficiency |\\n\\nNet effect on the distribution: S1 (confident fabrication) is throttled by mandatory evidence plus the `UNVERIFIED` tag; S3 (theater) is throttled by step 4's explicit permission to *not* name a cause; S5 and S6 become reachable. S2 stops being a failure mode and becomes a legitimate terminal state.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Evidence table\\n\\n| Key | Claim | Type | Where to verify | What would refute it |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **C1** | Claude Desktop's config uses top-level key `mcpServers`, mapping server name → config object | INFERENCE (recall) | docs.anthropic.com / modelcontextprotocol.io quickstart for Claude Desktop | Official docs specify a different top-level key, or accept multiple |\\n| **C2** | stdio entries require `command` (string); `args` must be an array; `env` an object | INFERENCE (recall) | Same as C1; MCP spec transport section | Docs show `command` optional, or a valid entry without it |\\n| **C3** | The \\"…were skipped\\" message is *schema validation* at load, distinct from runtime start/connect failure — a missing binary produces a different symptom | INFERENCE (recall) | Reproduce: (a) entry with valid shape + nonexistent command; (b) entry with malformed shape. Compare messages and `mcp-server-*.log` | Both cases produce the identical \\"skipped\\" message ⇒ my main discriminator collapses and the rewrite's step 1 is misleading |\\n| **C4** | Claude Desktop's JSON config historically rejected remote entries (`url` / `type: http|sse`); remote servers went via Settings → Connectors | ASSUMPTION | Anthropic docs for the user's specific build + release notes; test a minimal `url` entry | Current build accepts `url` in the JSON file ⇒ a whole hypothesis branch is void. **Version-dependent; I would not act on this without checking** |\\n| **C5** | `skyhook-io/radar` exists as described and exposes an MCP server; its invocation syntax | OPEN | github.com/skyhook-io/radar — README, `radar --help`, releases | Repo doesn't exist / different owner / no MCP server / different transport. **I cannot confirm any part of this from recall** |\\n| **C6** | A whole-file JSON parse error yields a *different* symptom than the per-entry skip message (config ignored entirely / different warning) | INFERENCE | Insert a trailing comma, restart, compare messages | Trailing comma produces the same per-entry \\"skipped: radar\\" ⇒ the file-vs-entry partition in